        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet: Require the descriptors flag when the FLAGS record is missing\n\nLoadWalletFlags only checked for WALLET_FLAG_DESCRIPTORS when the\ndatabase had a FLAGS record. A SQLite wallet file without that record\nwas loaded with no flags set and then handled as a legacy wallet,\nwhich ends in an Assert:\n\n- with a legacy record, in SetupLegacyDataSPKM, because the database\n  is not bdb_ro\n- otherwise in LoadActiveScriptPubKeyMan, because the descriptors\n  flag is not set\n\nloadwallet aborts the node on such a file, and with the wallet in the\nload on startup list the node no longer starts.\n\nDo the check whether or not the record exists, so the file is\nrejected as a legacy wallet. Nothing loads a database without the\nrecord anymore now that the wallet tool does not load on create. The\nunit tests that load a hand written database write the flags first.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jan Kahmen <jan@turingpoint.de>",
      "committer": {
